/E (A wildcard mask is a 32-bit binary mask used in networking to determine which bits of an IP address to check or ignore when filtering traffic or defining networks. It is often called an inverted subnet mask, where 0 bits mean "must match" and 1 bits mean "ignore" \(don't care\).)
